# SABOTAGE: R7's WIP boundary is dropped — every location's stock counts as WIP.
#
# WS-ACCT Phase 4 (ADR-054 D3) makes "WIP – Foundry" a GL PRESENTATION of stock
# held at a `kind: :supplier` warehouse, never a second register. R7
# (`Samen.Scopes.Inventory.ReconcileLot`) reads exactly that boundary: supplier-
# location stock value per lot == the WIP balance the journal carries for the
# lot. This patch removes ONLY the `AND w.<kind> = 'supplier'` predicate from the
# stock side, keeping the lot anchor (`source_key = 'lot'`), the WIP-account
# join, the posted-entry join and every other leg.
#
# That is the plausible regression, not a strawman: a reviewer reading the read
# sees a ledger sum grouped by lot and a GL sum grouped by lot's cost object and
# concludes the warehouse kind is a detail. It is not — it is the whole WIP
# definition. With it gone, stock the company already OWNS (a delivered lot, or
# wafers a partner holds on consignment where title moved at shipment) is
# reported as work-in-progress, and the books claim WIP that no supplier holds.
#
# Why the flip is attributable: the two red-path tests (supplier stock with no
# GL leg, and a WIP balance with no stock) STILL fail under this patch — the
# predicate was never what made a real disagreement visible. Only the two
# boundary controls red, which is what says the flip landed on the WIP
# definition rather than on the ledger, the GL or the test file.
#
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/inventory_lots_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: owned stock is NOT WIP — a delivered lot reconciles clean
# MUST_FAIL: consignment stock is NOT supplier WIP — it reconciles clean
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/scopes/inventory/reconcile_lot.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/scopes/inventory/reconcile_lot.ex
@@ -113,9 +113,8 @@
       JOIN #{ctx.warehouse_table} w
         ON w.#{ctx.warehouse_id} = sl.#{ctx.ledger_warehouse}
        AND w.#{ctx.warehouse_org} = sl.#{ctx.ledger_org}
       WHERE sl.#{ctx.ledger_org} = $1
         AND sl.#{ctx.ledger_source_key} = 'lot'
-        AND w.#{ctx.warehouse_kind} = 'supplier'
       GROUP BY sl.#{ctx.ledger_source_id}
     ) stock ON stock.lot_id = l.#{ctx.lot_id}
     """
